[[ ## document ## ]]
{
  "title": "Kestrel Manufacturing — June 2025 Inventory Tie-Out: Accrual Policy Note & Vendor Credit Memo Summary",
  "path": "engagements/kestrel-manufacturing/inventory/2025-06-accrual-policy-and-credit-memo-summary.docx",
  "document": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 1,
        "text": "Kestrel Manufacturing — June 2025 Inventory Tie-Out Support"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Prepared by Nadia Osman for Victor and Theo. This note supports the June 2025 inventory tie-out by documenting (1) the 2025 accrual policy applicable to inventory-related accruals and (2) the vendor credit memo identified for June, including its impact on the inventory balance."
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "1. 2025 Accrual Policy Note"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Per the Kestrel 2025 accounting policy manual (Section 3.2 — Accruals), the following rules apply to inventory-related accruals for the 2025 fiscal year:"
      },
      {
        "kind": "list",
        "ordered": true,
        "items": [
          "Goods received but not yet invoiced (GRNI) are accrued at the lower of the purchase order value or the most recent vendor quote, with a corresponding credit to accrued liabilities and debit to inventory.",
          "Accruals are reversed in the month following receipt of the vendor invoice, in line with the recurring accrual policy (Section 3.2.4).",
          "Freight and customs charges related to inventory in transit are accrued if the goods have shipped FOB destination and title has transferred, using an estimated freight percentage of 2.5% of the purchase value unless a specific carrier rate is available.",
          "Rebates and vendor credits are recognized as a reduction of inventory cost when the credit memo is received and the underlying goods have been sold or remain in inventory, consistent with the net inventory valuation policy.",
          "Any accrual exceeding $50,000 requires manager approval and documented support; otherwise, the accrual is capped at $50,000 per vendor per month."
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "2. Vendor Credit Memo Summary — June 2025"
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "One vendor credit memo was identified during the June 2025 inventory tie-out. Details are as follows:"
      },
      {
        "kind": "table",
        "columns": ["Field", "Detail"],
        "rows": [
          ["Credit memo number", "CM-2025-0417"],
          ["Vendor", "Northgate Steel Supply Co."],
          ["Issue date", "June 18, 2025"],
          ["Reference", "PO #K-88231 — steel coil shipment received May 2025"],
          ["Credit amount", "$38,420.00"],
          ["Reason", "Price adjustment — vendor invoiced at $1,240/ton vs. agreed $1,190/ton for 768 tons"],
          ["Inventory treatment", "Reduction of inventory cost (steel raw materials)"],
          ["Posting status", "Posted to June 2025 general ledger; GL account 1200-RAW (inventory) credited, GL account 4110-VEND (vendor rebates) debited"],
          ["Supporting documentation", "Signed purchase order amendment dated May 3, 2025; vendor credit memo; receiving report RR-5512"]
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "3. Impact on June Inventory Tie-Out"
      },
      {
        "kind": "list",
        "ordered": false,
        "items": [
          "The credit memo reduces the June 30, 2025 raw materials inventory balance by $38,420.",
          "No accrual reversal is required for this credit memo — it is a direct reduction of inventory cost, not a reversal of a GRNI accrual.",
          "The credit memo does not affect the June GRNI accrual balance, which remains at $214,730 as per the June accrual schedule (detailed in the tie-out workbook).",
          "Net effect on inventory: $38,420 reduction in raw materials; no change to work-in-progress or finished goods.",
          "This credit memo was not previously recorded in the May 2025 inventory balance, so no restatement is required."
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "4. Follow-Up Items"
      },
      {
        "kind": "list",
        "ordered": false,
        "items": [
          "Confirm with Northgate that the credit memo has been applied to the June 30 statement of account (email sent June 25, awaiting reply).",
          "Verify that the corresponding vendor invoice (INV-2025-0912) has been adjusted in the accounts payable subledger — finance team to confirm by July 2.",
          "Flag for the Q3 margin review: the $38,420 reduction will flow through to cost of goods sold when the underlying steel is used in production, expected in July production runs."
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "If you need the underlying support (credit memo PDF, PO amendment, or GL screenshot), they are saved in the engagement folder under engagements/kestrel-manufacturing/inventory/support/2025-06/. Happy to walk through anything on a call."
      },
      {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Nadia Osman — Staff Accountant"
      }
    ]
  }
}
